+# Harry-Chen FP4 SM120 algorithm attribution
+
+Upstream project: Harry-Chen/fp4_sm120  
+Repository: https://github.com/Harry-Chen/fp4_sm120  
+License: Apache License 2.0; the upstream license is included verbatim in `LICENSE` beside this notice.
+
+The stochastic dither algorithm and random-byte arrangement in
+`src/spalmer/experts/nvfp4_sm120.py` were adapted from the published
+`stochastic_rounding/sr.sm120.cuh` implementation. Its original author is
+attributed to the upstream Harry-Chen project. SPALMER expresses the algorithm
+in Triton, integrates it with TorchAO's existing conversion interface, explicitly
+maps every NaN to positive E2M1 maximum, supplies CPU reference tests, and scopes
+the compatibility override to an exclusive eager-execution context. These are
+SPALMER adaptations; the upstream file is not copied verbatim into the runtime.
+
+This notice applies to that adaptation only. It does not change the license of
+SPALMER as a whole. No claim is made that this adaptation is endorsed by the
+upstream author, NVIDIA, or PyTorch, or is bit-identical to SM100 hardware.
+
+The upstream snapshot consulted for this attribution is commit `0a732dad1a26399797691ac1131abaf763037acb`:
+
+- Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Harry-Chen/fp4_sm120/0a732dad1a26399797691ac1131abaf763037acb/stochastic_rounding/sr.sm120.cuh
+- Source SHA256: `8d8cbbfa290ea4f34cb0c79074bcbb8e668e10afe8cb161da16451f7f6f8a5c5`
+- License SHA256: `cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30`
+- Root-level upstream NOTICE files found at this revision: none.
+
+The source header itself contains no additional copyright or attribution notice.
+The full upstream license has been preserved without substituting a new author
+into its generic license-application appendix.
